<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hassan Tower</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hassan Tower is the unfinished minaret of a great mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabat">Rabat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>, begun under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-al-mansur">Yaqub al-Mansur</a> in the late twelfth century. The mosque was never completed. The tower is counted with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koutoubia-mosque">Koutoubia Mosque</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giralda">Giralda</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> among the finest monuments of the Almohad Caliphate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hassan-tower.jpg" alt="Hassan Tower" width="307" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hassan_Tower,_Rabat,_Marocco_(%D8%B5%D9%88%D9%85%D8%B9%D8%A9_%D8%AD%D8%B3%D8%A7%D9%86_).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
